        "like": 5
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I concur; this would be a Godsend for accessibility.\nI'd also like to add a similar feature to the \"Vive Advanced Control\", allowing you to lock the trigger to outputting a gesture that you previously held. This would tie into use with the trackpad. (Peace sign on trackpad + trigger = rebinding trigger to peace sign)\nThis is a legacy behavior with Vive wands, but was immensely helpful for triggering things such as a gesture that makes a gun shoot. Not every avatar creator uses the same gesture to preform the action, and allowing you to essentially rebind the trigger on the fly was immensely helpful.\nFor me in particular, I use this for very quickly puppeteering facial expressions on my avatar. I would not normally be able to trigger them nearly as quickly without it. Something like this on Index (if it doesn't already exist) would also be helpful on index if they initially listen to the trackpad for that behavior.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-06-07T22:47:28.198Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I would like to be able to read the input float value for the joystick and track-pad respectively.\nThis would allow things like a \"legacy\" gesture system to be created on Index controllers, where you could trigger different animations by sliding your thumb around on the track-pad, rather than relying on the finger tracking.",
